      "content": "thanks. the \"Safe Bet\" notes are good, they show that very predictable, risk-averse energy.\n\nnow, can you finish Scenario 2? i really need that \"High-Impact Maverick\" dialogue and the corresponding \"Private Risk Assessment.\"\n\nremember, for the notes on the Maverick, i'm looking for that very specific, \"professional-sounding\" way a board of directors might subtly disqualify them. they'll definitely admit the person is a genius or a powerhouse, but then they'll use that high-level, coded language to suggest they just don't have the \"boardroom presence\" or \"executive poise\" required.\n\ni'm looking for terms like \"potential for cultural friction,\" \"lacks a subtle touch,\" \"stylistic misalignment with the brand,\" or \"questions regarding long-term stability/gravitas.\" i want to see how they use those descriptors to pivot from \"amazing performer\" to \"not ready for the C-suite.\"",
